  "problem": "",
  "worked_solution": "The number of permutations of $n$ objects taken $r$ at a time is given by the formula\n\n$$\n{}_{n}{P}_{r}=\\frac{n!}{(n-r)!}.\n$$\n\nThere are $40$ marbles to choose from, so $n=40.$ We want to select $5$ of those marbles for the line, so we have $r=5.$ \n\nTherefore, the number of different ways to line up $5$ marbles is \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{}_{40}{P}_{5} & =\\frac{40!}{(40-5)!} \\\\  & =\\frac{40!}{35!} \\\\  & =\\frac{40\\cdot 39\\cdot 38\\cdot 37\\cdot 36\\cdot \\cancel{35!}}{\\cancel{35!}} \\\\  & =40\\cdot 39\\cdot 38\\cdot 37\\cdot 36 \\\\  & =78\\,960\\,960.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
  "calculator_instructions": "",
